<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thiệu Trị</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1807–1847</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Thieu Tri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thiệu Trị was the third emperor of the Nguyen dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, ruling from 1841 to 1847 after his father Minh Mạng. Faced with revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>, he withdrew Vietnamese forces from much of the country, accepting shared influence with Siam. He continued restrictions on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a>, and in 1847 French warships attacked Vietnamese vessels at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/da-nang">Da Nang</a> shortly before his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thieu-tri.jpg" alt="Thiệu Trị" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_lang_Thieu_Tri_CdM.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
